          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "τὸ σὲ οἰκονομεῖν ἀναδέξασθαι χάριν οἶδα εἰληφώς, οὐ δεδωκώς",
          "english_quote": "Hence I know that, in your undertaking to administer, I have received a favor, not given one.",
          "issue": "The notes disclose two infinitival analyses but omit another materially relevant possibility: σέ may be the object of οἰκονομεῖν, with the speaker undertaking to direct or make provision for Clement. The draft's assignment of the undertaking to Clement therefore remains less fully qualified than the notes suggest.",
          "suggested_revision": "Expand source_issues to distinguish σέ as an infinitival subject from σέ as the object of οἰκονομεῖν. Compare the resulting accounts of who undertakes what and who receives the favor before choosing revised English. Preserve the supplied reading; this is a syntactic and interpretive problem, not an established transcription defect.",
