          "source_quote": "αὐτὸν διαλλάττων σώζηται, τῆς αὐτοῦ ἐπακούων ὁμιλίας",
          "english_quote": "may be saved by reconciling him and heeding his discourse",
          "issue": "The pronoun referents and the precise reconciliation relationship remain unresolved. The English preserves the pronouns, and the source_issues disclose the uncertainty; acceptance of this rendering does not establish either referent.",
          "suggested_revision": "Retain the unresolved source_issues and the unexpanded pronouns. Any later wording that identifies the person reconciled or the speaker whose discourse is heard must undergo fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "reference": "19",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": true,
        "no_added_claims": true,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "lexical_fidelity": false,
        "uncertainties_disclosed": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "Ἀξιῶ σε ἐπὶ πάντων μου τῶν συνπαρόντων ἀδελφῶν, ὅπως ὁπόταν τοῦ ἐνταῦθα (ὡς ἐμοὶ ὀφείλεται) ἀπαλλάξω βίου, σὲ Ἰακώβῳ τῷ ἀδελφῷ τοῦ κυρίου διαπέμψαι ἐν ἐπιτομῇ ἀναγραψάμενον μέχρι καὶ τῶν ἐκ παίδων σου λογισμῶν καὶ ὡς ἀπ᾽ ἀρχῆς μέχρι τοῦ νῦν συνώδευσάς μοι, ἐπακούων τῶν κατὰ πόλιν ὑπ᾽ ἐμοῦ κηρυχθέντων λόγων τε καὶ πράξεων, ἔπειτα πρὸς τῷ τέλει καὶ τὴν τοῦ θανάτου μου πρόφασιν ὡς προεῖπον δηλῶσαι μὴ ὀκνήσῃς",
          "english_quote": "Then, toward the end, do not hesitate also to make known the cause of my death, as I foretold.",
          "issue": "The draft attaches “do not hesitate” explicitly only to disclosing the death's cause. A substantial alternative is that the concluding μὴ ὀκνήσῃς governs both διαπέμψαι and δηλῶσαι within the request introduced by ὅπως. On that analysis, Clement must not hesitate either to send the account or to disclose the cause. The existing syntax note acknowledges unresolved relations, but the main text adopts the narrower scope.",
          "suggested_revision": "Explicitly compare the current distribution with a construction beginning “I ask you … not to hesitate to send … and then, toward the end, also to make known …”. Retain the uncertainty concerning the resumed σέ and the extended construction until that comparison is reviewed. Do not treat this proposed restructuring as accepted English or alter the supplied Greek punctuation.",
          "severity": "major"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "reference": "20",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": true,
        "no_added_claims": true,
        "names_and_negations": true,
